  "details": "I have tried creating a 2D Audiosource for my Avatar.\nThe Problem i am facing is that, whenever i try and make the 2D Audio fall off to Zero after a certain distance, InGame it just continues, ignoring the Volume Curve entirely.\nNow i have tried using the spatial curve to make it transition from 2D to 3D audio after a certain distance, which works fine in Unity and the Audio stops after i am a certain distance away from the source, but In VRChat yet again this gets ignored and the volume continues unhindered.\nI have created 2 test Avatars both have \"Enable Spatialization\" turned off in the vrc Component.\nThe First is using 100% 2D Audio that rolls off to 0 Volume after 5 Meters.\navtr_aa1e0873-637a-48de-a71e-22e401b2eb41\nThe Second having the same Settings, only now with the Spatial Curve edited to switch back to 3D after 5 Meters.\navtr_3711d5cd-c62d-4bb3-8a40-275c35d8c19f\nI have also noticed that the first method does not seem to work in Unity itself (Audio continues after 6 Meters)\nbut the Second method works in Unity atleast (Audio is 2D and stops after 6 Meters)\nHope this helps! :)",
